# Phase 2 — Mechanical baseline system

This is one of the unique RoboBladez mechanics.

For each matchup:

```text
body A
vs
body B
```

run neutral/passive or standardized-control simulations.

Generate:

```text
MechanicalMatchupReport
```

Example:

```json
{
  "a": "boris-body-v3",
  "b": "morty-body-v2",

  "neutral_runs": 1000,

  "win_probability": {
    "a": 0.31,
    "b": 0.61,
    "draw": 0.08
  },

  "advantages": {
    "a": [
      "higher spin endurance",
      "better center stability"
    ],
    "b": [
      "higher mobility",
      "better contact acceleration"
    ]
  },

  "vulnerabilities": {
    "a": ["rim chase"],
    "b": ["late spin-out"]
  }
}
```

Both agents receive this before committing strategy.

That makes the match about **reasoning against known mechanical asymmetry**.

### Exit condition

You can demonstrate:

> weaker body wins because policy exploited opponent/body tendencies.

That is a defining RoboBladez moment.

