# Phase 4 — Sandboxed competitors

Only now make external policies possible.

Architecture:

```text
MATCH SERVER
     │
     ├── competitor process A
     └── competitor process B
```

Protocol:

```text
Observation JSON
↓
competitor
↓
Action JSON
```

Enforce:

```text
CPU limit
memory limit
wall-clock timeout
no network
no arbitrary filesystem
deterministic runtime
```

Competitor timeout:

```text
→ idle action
```

Repeated violation:

```text
→ match penalty / forfeit
```

This is where Robocode Tank Royale is the best precedent:

[https://github.com/robocode-dev/tank-royale](https://github.com/robocode-dev/tank-royale)

### Exit condition

You can run two untrusted competitor packages without either touching the game process.

