# Phase 6 — Agent learning

Start simple.

## 6.1 Opponent modelling

Every competitor stores:

```text
opponent aggression
center preference
energy usage
opening pattern
response to pressure
late-round behavior
```

Use Bayesian-ish counts or EWMA.

No neural network required.

Example:

```text
P(Morty rushes opening) = .72
P(Morty retreats after losing R1) = .61
```

## 6.2 Post-match reflection

Generate structured data:

```json
{
  "match": "...",
  "predictions": {
    "rush_probability": 0.72
  },
  "observed": {
    "rushed": true
  },
  "successful_actions": [],
  "failed_assumptions": [],
  "proposed_changes": []
}
```

This can initially be deterministic analytics.

LLM can later summarize/interpret.

## 6.3 Parameter evolution

Let agents mutate:

```text
thresholds
utility weights
opening strategy
energy budget allocation
fallback branches
```

Use evolutionary search.

Example:

```text
parent policy
↓
8 mutations
↓
evaluate against historical opponents
↓
select robust offspring
```

Do not automatically pick “highest current win rate.”

Use robustness:

```text
fitness =
win rate
− exploitability
+ diversity
+ robustness
```

